 "text": "Google just made Gemini Tasks free, and this is big news. Tasks is Gemini's AI agent. Instead of just chatting, you hand it a job, it works on it in the background, and it pings you when it's done. For example, I can flip Gemini from Chat to Task and type, watch flights from New York to Lagos in December, and tell me when one drops under $900. It checks the prices every morning, compares the airlines, and sends me a notification the moment the price drops. But here's the part most people are missing. In the US, it can now call businesses for you to compare quotes, it can buy things with Google Pay once you approve, and you can even text it like a friend. And it's free in the US, Canada, Japan, South Korea, Australia, and India, on your phone, your Mac, and the web. Before this, you had to pay for Pro or Ultra. The one thing I'd watch out for, it can read your email, your calendar, and your saved passwords to get things done. It asks before it buys or sends anything, but set a spending cap, and don't hit always allow on everything. But think about what this means, hundreds of millions of people just got a free assistant that does the boring stuff while they're busy living. If you wanna try it, comment TASKS, and I'll send you the link, plus 10 tasks you can hand it today."
